Phase OS-15: Kernel Memory Management Enhancements - 3 new AArch64 assembly kernel modules:

1. kernel/mem_paging.asm (Virtual Memory Paging)
   - Base ID: 907
   - Virtual memory paging with page tables and TLB management
   - Features: page table management (3-level), page allocation/deallocation, TLB invalidation, page protection (read/write/execute), page fault handling, demand paging, copy-on-write support, page frame tracking
   - Data structures: page_table_t (pml4_addr, level, entry_count, flags), page_entry_t (phys_addr, flags, ref_count, dirty, accessed), tlb_entry_t (vaddr, paddr, asid, valid)
   - API: mem_paging_init, mem_paging_create_table, mem_paging_map, mem_paging_unmap, mem_paging_protect, mem_paging_tlb_flush, mem_paging_get_phys, mem_paging_page_fault
   - Capacity: 4096 page tables, 65536 TLB entries, 4KB pages
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style (stp/ldp frame, .global exports, .bss for state)

2. kernel/mem_swap.asm (Swap Space Management)
   - Base ID: 908
   - Swap space management for virtual memory extension
   - Features: swap area initialization, page swap out/in, swap slot allocation/deallocation, swap statistics, swap priority, swap cluster management, synchronous/asynchronous swap I/O, swap encryption
   - Data structures: swap_area_t (dev_id, start_block, num_blocks, free_slots, priority, encrypted), swap_slot_t (page_frame, swap_offset, in_use, dirty)
   - API: mem_swap_init, mem_swap_add_area, mem_swap_out, mem_swap_in, mem_swap_alloc_slot, mem_swap_free_slot, mem_swap_stats, mem_swap_reclaim
   - Capacity: 4 swap areas, 16384 slots per area, 4KB per slot
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

3. kernel/mem_cache.asm (Page Cache Management)
   - Base ID: 909
   - Page cache for file system and block device caching
   - Features: cache entry management, LRU eviction, read-ahead, write-back, cache statistics, cache invalidation, dirty page tracking, synchronous flush, cache quotas per filesystem
   - Data structures: cache_entry_t (block_num, dev_id, page_frame, dirty, accessed, lru_next, lru_prev, ref_count), cache_stats_t (hits, misses, evictions, writebacks)
   - API: mem_cache_init, mem_cache_read, mem_cache_write, mem_cache_flush, mem_cache_invalidate, mem_cache_stats, mem_cache_reclaim, mem_cache_set_quota
   - Capacity: 8192 cache entries, 64MB total cache, 4KB per entry
   - Pattern: follow kernel/memory.asm style

Build all 3 kernel modules with:
  clang --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu -c -O2 -o kernel/<name>.o kernel/<name>.asm

